add('3c3a53',9,2.5,'Combinatorics',['optimization'],'The inequality k²+2≥3(k+1)/2 gives the sharp bound; moves k=0,1 attain it.')
add('8af34c',9,6.5,'Geometry',['orthocentre','vectors','Ceva theorem'],'Reflection identifies the side points; Ceva and the vector equation force medians.',r'An acute triangle $ABC$ has circumcentre $O$, radius $R$, and orthocentre $H$. Choose $A_1\in BC$, $B_1\in CA$, $C_1\in AB$ satisfying $HA_1+A_1O=HB_1+B_1O=HC_1+C_1O=R$. If $\overrightarrow{AA_1}+\overrightarrow{BB_1}+\overrightarrow{CC_1}=0$, prove $ABC$ is equilateral.',2)
add('418c63',9,6,'Algebra',['floor function','integer bounds'],'Reduce to integer candidates, then constrain them to an interval shorter than one.',r'For $n\ge2$, consider $\sum_{j=1}^{n}\{jx\}=\sum_{j=1}^{2n}\lfloor jx\rfloor$. Solve it for $n=2$, and prove it has at most two real solutions for every $n$.',3)
add('2d99cd',9,6.5,'Algebra',['sequences','summation by parts'],'Block estimates and repeated weighted telescoping control three successive moments.',r'Fix an integer $m\ge2$. Nonnegative reals $a_n$ satisfy $a_{n+1}\le a_n-a_{mn}$ for all $n\ge1$. Prove that both $\sum_{k=1}^n a_k$ and $\sum_{k=1}^n k^2a_k$ are bounded above independently of $n$.',4)
add('27ace7',10,6.5,'Geometry',['complex numbers','Simson line'],'Unit-circle reflection formulas prove collinearity and constrain the common centroid.',r'Reflect a point $M\notin\{A,B,C\}$ across the sidelines of triangle $ABC$, obtaining $N,P,Q$. Prove they are collinear exactly when $M$ lies on the circumcircle. Otherwise, prove that equal centroids of $ABC$ and $NPQ$ force $ABC$ equilateral.')
add('b6f1bf',10,5.5,'Combinatorics',['incidence counting','extremal construction'],'Count rich lines through points; a generic line arrangement achieves equality.',r'Fix $n\ge1$. In a finite planar point set $S$, call two points connected if their line contains exactly $n+1$ points of $S$. Find the smallest $|S|$ when every point is connected to exactly $2n$ others.',2)
